# Council-gate protected paths — CIB-149 follow-up.
#
# Commits touching these save-time authorisation / confinement surfaces are
# ALWAYS gated on a converged Council review by `.claude/hooks/council-gate.sh`,
# regardless of CLAUDE_COUNCIL_GATE and regardless of `--no-verify` / `--amend`,
# so an autonomous workflow cannot land a same-uid trust-boundary change past
# its own escalation signal. A human may deliberately override a block with
# `CLAUDE_COUNCIL_GATE_OVERRIDE=i-reviewed-this` (loud, logged, never a default).
#
# Rationale: ADR-097 (allowlist confinement admits only explicit entries) and
# `plans/reviews/post-merge/fix-cib-149-verified-primary-root-allowlist.md` — CIB-149's
# fail-closed fix self-corrected twice inside one autonomous run and then merged
# past its own escalation recommendation; this list makes that structurally
# harder for the trust surface it touched.
#
# Format: one glob per line; `#` starts a comment. Matching supports exact
# paths, shell globs (`*`), and directory prefixes. Tune this list as the trust
# surface moves — keep it narrow (auth/confinement only), not the whole crate.

crates/anvil-intercept/src/confinement.rs
crates/anvil-intercept/src/save_time.rs
crates/anvil-intercept/src/ipc.rs
crates/anvil-intercept/src/workspace_admission.rs
crates/anvil-intercept/src/auth.rs
crates/anvil-intercept/src/registry.rs
